,"year":2021,"counterion":"O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F.O=S(=O)([O-])C(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-004681","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Solutions of 1, 2, 3, and 4 (25 µm) were prepared in 3 mL octanol in separate screw cap glass vials. Deionized H2O (3 mL) was added, and the vials were capped and wrapped in foil. The vials were shaken vigorously for 5 min before allowing to settle overnight (~18 h). Triplicate absorbance measurement was taken for both the octanol and water layers of each vial for each compound. LogPo/w was calculated by first solving for the quotient of the absorbance in octanol over the absorbance in water and then taking the common logarithm. Three LogPo/w values were calculated for each compound, and those values were averaged to produce the average LogPo/w values shown in Table 1, where errors are the standard deviation of the three values."}]}